    "kicker": "Why this model / how we trained it",
    "title": "A small model. A deliberate choice.",
    "seconds": 40,
    "notes": "We kept a linear ranker because gradient boosting did not improve our held-out results. For baseline training, each shown product becomes an example; unshown products are not labeled failures. Clicks provide more examples, while purchases receive three times the weight. We model slot position because exposure changes behavior. We reconstruct earlier shopper state and test on later requests. The final policy then combines cohort-specific refits and overrides, rather than blindly deploying the default training output.",
    "source": "recsys/lfm_build.py: impressions(), fit(), BUY_W=3, log-slot and regularized LogisticRegression. Purchase calibration supports reports, not a guarantee for overridden final scores. R-24/E-260 documents the held-out gradient-boosting comparison. As-of metadata limitations remain in the replay reports.",
