  {
    "kicker": "Why this adaptation / how it stays stable",
    "title": "Frozen weights. Live intelligence.",
    "seconds": 35,
    "notes": "We separated changing evidence from stable model weights. Shopper memory updates as people return, including new shoppers without historical profiles. Product quality uses organic views and purchases; recommendation purchases update user memory, not the organic rate. That separation prevents a feedback loop. Trends come from recent events versus a baseline, not yesterday's clock. This lets us adapt during the final without refitting on a handful of noisy purchases. Previous purchases still stay excluded.",
