    "notes": "Offline screening was not enough, because logged impressions reflect what earlier policies chose to show. For live checks, we compared against the reference in the same windows, so a better hour would not look like a better model. Across eight practice blocks, refitted weights showed a zero-point-seventeen percentage-point improvement, with ten thousand eight hundred requests per policy. These were time blocks, not randomized A/B. We also rejected ideas and wrote counterexamples when passing tests missed real query behavior.",
